WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.420
<v Instructor>So just a quick lecture around S3 Analytics.</v>

2
00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:06.090
And in the exam you may see it being called

3
00:00:06.090 --> 00:00:10.740
just Storage Class Analysis, so these two are equivalent.

4
00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:13.290
And it's a feature to help you decide

5
00:00:13.290 --> 00:00:17.100
when to transition objects into the right storage class.

6
00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:20.130
So it's going to give you recommendations to transition data

7
00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:23.370
for the Standard and the Standard IA storage class,

8
00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:26.400
but it doesn't work for One-Zone IA or Glacier.

9
00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:29.400
It's a report that's updated daily and it may take

10
00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:33.720
between 24 to 48 hours to start seeing the data

11
00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:37.320
and analyze it within the S3 buckets

12
00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:39.900
You can also visualize all of its data

13
00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:43.410
into Amazon QuickSight, which has integrations

14
00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:45.540
with this dataset.

15
00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:48.960
So using the Storage Class Analysis feature

16
00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:52.080
is a really good first step to put together Lifecycle Rules

17
00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:55.050
or to improve them and to figure out the sweet spot.

18
00:00:55.050 --> 00:00:57.450
To summarize, we have our S3 bucket

19
00:00:57.450 --> 00:01:00.660
and we have Storage Class Analysis on top of it,

20
00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:04.740
And then after a while, a CS report is going to be created,

21
00:01:04.740 --> 00:01:08.580
which gives us insight into which storage class we have

22
00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:12.960
in our bucket on which object as well as the age and so on.

23
00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:13.950
So that's it for this lecture.

24
00:01:13.950 --> 00:01:17.013
I hope you liked it, and I will see you in the next lecture.

